                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p> Second son of John Brown (1738-1788), an innovative medical doctor from
                            a very poor background. Ford Brown married Caroline Madox . Ford was a
                            purser on the Arethusa, but retired after the Napoleonic Wars - and they
                            lived in reduced circumstance (in part in Calais), which marked the upbringing of their son,
                            Ford Maddox Ford (1821-1893). Brother of William Cullen Brown, who also appears in the diary. </p>
